[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Independent Circuit Consistency Audits

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
This bounded audit profile supplements numerical residuals with element-level physical checks. Passing checks establish consistency within recorded tolerances, not model validity, uniqueness, global waveform accuracy or production qualification. Iterations 311-320 implement this profile; broader sparse, model and ngspice qualification remains active.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: CONS-001
TITLE: Explicit bounded audit evidence
STATEMENT: >>>
Audits shall expose passed, failed and not_checked outcomes with SI discrepancy, effective tolerance and a reason when unavailable. Invalid tolerance settings shall be rejected and nonfinite check arithmetic shall fail with JSON-safe null metrics.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: src/audit.rs Check, AuditOptions and AuditReport. Verification: tests/consistency.rs::audit_metrics_are_json_safe_and_bounds_are_validated.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-VERIFY-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: CONS-002
TITLE: Independent DC current conservation
STATEMENT: >>>
The DC audit shall reconstruct supported element currents without assembled matrices or production model evaluation, check KCL at every node including ground, and reject malformed or nonfinite MNA states. Fixed Gmin shall be explicitly included with unregularized physics marked not_checked.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: src/audit.rs::dc and dc_currents. Verification: tests/consistency.rs::independent_kcl_detects_perturbed_current_and_rejects_malformed_states.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: CONS-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: CONS-003
TITLE: Independent voltage constraints
STATEMENT: >>>
The DC audit shall check independent voltage sources, VCVS, CCVS and DC inductor voltage constraints separately from KCL using voltage-dimensional bounds. A KCL-consistent state violating an ideal voltage source shall fail.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: src/audit.rs::constraint_checks. Verification: tests/consistency.rs voltage_constraint_catches_a_kcl_consistent_wrong_solution and controlled_voltage_and_inductor_constraints_are_audited.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: CONS-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: CONS-004
TITLE: DC power conservation
STATEMENT: >>>
The independent DC audit shall sum absorbed element power using passive sign convention and include explicit Gmin dissipation. It shall report a power-dimensional absolute-plus-relative bound and fail nonfinite arithmetic. Shunt-regularized success shall not imply an unregularized physical solution.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: src/audit.rs::power_check. Verification: tests/consistency.rs::power_audit_includes_shunt_dissipation_and_detects_wrong_source_current.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: CONS-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: CONS-005
TITLE: Bounded topology preflight
STATEMENT: >>>
Preflight shall identify directly conflicting parallel independent voltage sources with polarity normalization and warn about nodes lacking an obvious DC reference path. Connectivity warnings shall not reject explicitly initialized transient or controlled-source circuits. Diagnostics shall have stable codes, severity and affected identifiers; complete rank or DAE classification is outside this profile.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: src/topology.rs. Verification: tests/consistency.rs::topology_warns_about_capacitor_only_paths_and_identifies_source_conflicts.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-VERIFY-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: CONS-006
TITLE: Backward-Euler physical step audit
STATEMENT: >>>
For finite complete MNA states and positive timesteps with constant nominal sources, the audit shall independently check capacitor current, inductor voltage, KCL, source constraints and discrete energy balance. The energy identity shall include backward-Euler numerical dissipation, not assert exact continuous energy conservation. Waveform aggregation shall retain the worst normalized discrepancy per check with memory bounded by circuit size.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: src/audit.rs::backward_euler_step and AuditReport::merge_worst. Verification: tests/consistency.rs::backward_euler_energy_audit_includes_integration_dissipation.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: CONS-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: CONS-007
TITLE: Public audit and diagnostic evidence
STATEMENT: >>>
Successful API manifests shall include bounded preflight diagnostics and independent consistency checks. DC and legacy constant-source backward-Euler transient states shall be audited before derived signals are appended; failed physical checks shall return numerical_failure. AC/configured transient physical audits and global accuracy shall be explicitly not_checked. C# consumers shall receive typed additive result fields.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: src/api.rs and dotnet/Simulator.Client/Results.cs. Verification: tests/consistency.rs::manifests_distinguish_physical_checks_and_unavailable_evidence and dotnet/Simulator.Conformance/Program.cs typed audit checks.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: CONS-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: CONS-008
TITLE: Structured opt-in diagnostic logging
STATEMENT: >>>
Rust library code shall emit structured tracing events without installing a global subscriber. The CLI shall install a JSON stderr subscriber filtered by RUST_LOG with warn fallback and leave stdout as protocol JSON only. Events shall identify request/backend context, topology diagnostics, compilation size, audit completion, and bounded continuation stages; Newton iteration residuals shall require trace level. Events shall not dump raw netlists, solution vectors or whole requests.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: src/main.rs, src/api.rs and src/newton.rs; tracing and tracing-subscriber versions are locked in Cargo.lock. Verification: tests/consistency.rs::debug_logging_keeps_protocol_stdout_clean.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-GOAL-004

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: CONS-009
TITLE: Explicit timestep-refinement comparison
STATEMENT: >>>
The Rust audit API shall compare independently supplied coarse and finer waveforms for a selected voltage or current at exactly shared coarse times, rejecting malformed axes, nonfinite values, missing signals or mismatched stop times. It shall retain the worst normalized discrepancy and identify observed change as distinct from a rigorous global accuracy bound. It shall not silently rerun the solver or interpolate samples.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: src/audit.rs::compare_refinement. Verification: tests/consistency.rs::timestep_refinement_compares_shared_samples_without_claiming_global_accuracy.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: CONS-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: CONS-010
TITLE: Reproducible audit qualification and limits
STATEMENT: >>>
The audit slice shall retain independent analytic examples, corrupted-state and loose-Newton rejection, malformed-state fuzz-smoke and seeded properties, targeted isolated mutations, full checkpoint checks and actual coverage availability. Reported evidence shall distinguish physical consistency from global accuracy and model validity, and identify unsupported analysis profiles and instrumentation limitations.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: tests/consistency.rs, scripts/Mutation.cs, evidence/checkpoint-320.json and evidence/consistency-qualification.md. Authoritative runtime requirements are CONS-001 through CONS-009; this requirement does not infer complete M1 qualification.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-VERIFY-002
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-VERIFY-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: PROP-002
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Generated independent numerical oracles and retained failures
STATEMENT: >>>
Generated numerical campaigns shall compare bounded circuit results with independent analytical equations and retain minimized failing inputs and provider identity. Numerical hardening shall not silently relax independent backward-error or physical tolerances to hide generated failures. Any refinement shall be bounded and preserve explicit failure when verification does not pass.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Derived campaign requirement. Implementation: tests/property_campaign.rs and bounded QR refinement in src/backend.rs. The persisted divider case in tests/regressions/property_campaign.txt exposed componentwise backward-error rejection before refinement. Actual provider/domain evidence is recorded per checkpoint.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: PROP-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: MAN-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Managed native-transport boundary qualification
STATEMENT: >>>
The managed client shall reject malformed or unsupported native envelopes, inconsistent completion/error states and unexpected process exits. Request/output bounds and cancellation shall be tested against an isolated subprocess fixture as well as real-engine conformance. Synthetic fixture outcomes shall remain distinct from numerical simulator evidence.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Derived campaign requirement. Implementation: dotnet/Simulator.Client/Client.cs. Verification: dotnet/Simulator.Client.Tests/TransportContracts.cs and the test-only Simulator.TransportFixture project. Initial fixture tests cover supported/unsupported versions and malformed JSON; additional boundaries and coverage remain pending.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-VERIFY-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: END-001
TITLE: Bounded isolated endurance campaign
STATEMENT: >>>
A manual endurance target shall run a selected mutation campaign once, then changing-seed endurance batches within a configurable monotonic wall-clock budget capped at 24 hours with a five-hour default. It shall use an isolated source snapshot, reject overlapping supervised runs through an exclusive file lock, cap child-process runtimes and retained logs, and report completed cases separately from partial, timed-out or failed work. Compiler/test concurrency shall be bounded. Working source and tracked qualification reports shall not be modified by a campaign.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: Makefile, scripts/Endurance.cs and scripts/Run-Endurance.ps1. Verification: tests/Endurance.Tests.ps1 and evidence/endurance-qualification.md. OS-wide memory enforcement and cleanup after forced supervisor termination are not claimed.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-VERIFY-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: END-002
TITLE: Reproducible changing-seed endurance evidence
STATEMENT: >>>
The endurance harness shall explore bounded parser mutations, sparse layouts, independent analytic divider solutions and diode derivative cases using recorded seeds. Reports shall retain source hashes, revision/dirty state, tool versions, completed-case counts and replay seeds. Failure inputs shall be preserved, with bounded deletion minimization for parser panics. Each source archive shall remain available after later runs; interrupted work shall never be called passing or covered.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: tests/endurance.rs and scripts/Endurance.cs. Verification: manual deterministic seed replay, budget and overlap checks in evidence/endurance-qualification.md. This is seeded fuzz/property testing, not coverage-guided fuzzing or an exhaustive source-mutation campaign.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: END-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: END-003
TITLE: Nightly invocation and morning evidence review
STATEMENT: >>>
The user-authorized scheduled workflow shall start a hidden five-hour-budget campaign at local midnight and review its actual artifacts at 05:05 America/Los_Angeles. Startup and results review shall distinguish active, missing, failed, unfinished and budget-exhausted work; a configured schedule shall not be treated as an executed five-hour qualification run.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: local thread automations spice-nightly-endurance-campaign and spice-morning-endurance-results, invoking scripts/Run-Endurance.ps1. Verification: saved automation configurations and the hidden-worker startup checks retained in evidence/endurance-qualification.md. Local machine/app availability is required; the initial full overnight execution remains pending.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: END-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REM-001
TITLE: Configurable cross-host qualification bootstrap
STATEMENT: >>>
The qualification workflow shall accept a finite positive endurance budget up to 24 hours, defaulting to five hours, and provide PowerShell setup for Windows x64 and Ubuntu/Debian x64. It shall read pinned SDK/compiler/documentation-tool versions, configure process-local tool paths, use official installer sources and record acquisition hashes. Required administrator approval and private-repository authentication shall remain explicit prerequisites, not silently bypassed. Setup shall have a verification-only mode.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: scripts/Setup-Host.ps1, HostTools.ps1, Start-RemoteRun.ps1, Run-Endurance.ps1 and Endurance.cs. Verification: tests/Endurance.Tests.ps1, tests/Remote.Tests.ps1 and evidence/remote-workflow-qualification.md. A Linux implementation does not by itself establish Linux execution evidence.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: END-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REM-002
TITLE: Identifiable isolated remote result branches
STATEMENT: >>>
The remote workflow shall use a dedicated clean checkout and check publication access before long testing. It shall publish bounded allowlisted evidence to a unique remote-runs/platform-architecture-label/time-source-revision branch, preserving main and source files. Reports shall distinguish full qualification workflow execution from imported endurance-only evidence and preserve failed/unavailable/not-measured outcomes.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: scripts/Start-RemoteRun.ps1 and RemoteQualification.cs. Verification: tests/Remote.Tests.ps1 local bare-Git publication and rejection cases. Bootstrap refuses directories it did not create. No force push, automatic merge or credential-in-URL workflow is provided.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-RUN-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REM-003
TITLE: Bounded provenance-checked evidence export
STATEMENT: >>>
Remote publication shall verify finished endurance metadata against the checkout revision and declared source hashes, reject malformed or unsafe paths and dirty/stale source, and stage only a manifest and checksum file. The manifest shall be capped at 256 KiB and contain structured outcomes, source identity, tools, seeds, durations, coverage availability and log hashes. Raw logs, credentials, binaries, absolute work paths and large corpora shall remain local.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: scripts/RemoteQualification.cs. Verification: tests/Remote.Tests.ps1 synthetic local-Git fixtures; real-workflow and coverage scope recorded in evidence/remote-workflow-qualification.md. Evidence is reviewable run output, not a cryptographic attestation of test execution.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REM-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: END-004
TITLE: Recoverable checkpoint sharing contention
STATEMENT: >>>
Checkpoint replacement shall retry transient file access failures for at most two seconds, retain valid JSON and record retries. Permanent failures shall remain failures rather than silently losing evidence.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: scripts/Endurance.cs. Verification: scripts/Test-CheckpointContention.ps1 and evidence/checkpoint-contention.json deliberately deny delete sharing for 500 milliseconds during a live campaign.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: END-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: MUT-001
TITLE: Pinned generated Rust and managed mutation testing
STATEMENT: >>>
The qualification tooling shall run pinned cargo-mutants on owned Rust sources and pinned Stryker.NET on executable managed-client behavior through discoverable real-engine contracts. These maintained frameworks shall be the primary mutation phase, receiving at most half the remaining campaign budget before library-generated property batches. Hand-selected numerical mutations shall remain separate, explicitly selected supplemental regression evidence rather than consuming the default campaign before the frameworks. Rust round-robin shard selection shall be recorded and reproducible from the campaign seed.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: scripts/FrameworkMutations.cs, Endurance.cs, Setup-MutationTools.ps1, dotnet-tools.json, dotnet/Simulator.Client.Tests and shared ConformanceChecks.cs. Verification: evidence/framework-mutation-qualification.md. A candidate inventory is not a tested-mutant count; sharded/time-bounded work is not an exhaustive mutation campaign.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: END-001
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-VERIFY-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: MUT-002
TITLE: Separate mutation outcomes and bounded remote evidence
STATEMENT: >>>
Mutation evidence shall distinguish generated candidates, kills, survivors, uncovered code, timeouts, invalid/compile-error mutants, ignored/pending/unknown categories and unattempted candidates. Framework baseline/infrastructure failures shall remain failures; deadline interruption shall remain partial evidence. Reports shall retain tool pins, tested scope/shard, elapsed budget and native report/log hashes; raw framework artifacts shall remain local. Remote publication shall validate bounded framework-summary hashes and category counts before exporting allowlisted path-free fields.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: scripts/FrameworkMutations.cs, Endurance.cs and RemoteQualification.cs. Verification: tests/FrameworkMutations.Tests.ps1, tests/EnduranceFramework.Tests.ps1, tests/Remote.Tests.ps1, native framework runs and scoped coverage evidence. Timeouts are never counted as test-detected kills, even when a framework score includes them.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: MUT-001
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REM-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: PROP-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Maintained property runners with shrinking and replay
STATEMENT: >>>
Generated Rust and managed property campaigns shall use maintained property-testing libraries, bounded cases and process deadlines, record replay seeds and preserve minimized failing cases. Malformed inputs shall be exercised without treating graceful rejection as successful numerical simulation. Library configuration and actual execution shall be reported separately.
<<<
